# Profile Page UI & Functionality Fixes

This plan addresses the oversized buttons on the profile page and resolves the issue where profile edits are not saving correctly or not providing feedback.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> I will be reducing the default padding and font size for buttons on the profile page to make them feel more compact. If you prefer a specific pixel size for buttons, let me know!

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] UI Enhancements (CSS & View)

#### [MODIFY] [modern.css](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/assets/css/modern.css)
- Add a `.modern-btn-sm` class for more compact buttons.
- Slightly reduce default `modern-btn` padding for better balance.

#### [MODIFY] [profile.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/customer/profile.php)
- Add a flashdata `'error'` alert block to show validation errors (this is likely why the edit "isn't working").
- Apply smaller button classes to "Edit Profile", "Sign Out", and "Save Changes" buttons.
- Ensure the modal correctly captures all fields.

### [Component] Profile Update Logic (Controller)

#### [MODIFY] [Customer.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Customer.php)
- Add explicit validation rules for `city`, `state`, and `zip_code` to ensure they are sanitized and handled correctly.
- Add logging or improved error handling if `update_customer` fails.

## Open Questions
- Is there a specific error message you see, or does the page just reload without changes? (Adding the error alert will help us find out!)

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- N/A (Manual visual check and form submission)

### Manual Verification
1. Login as a customer.
2. Navigate to [Profile](http://localhost/coolex_shop/Customer/profile).
3. Verify button sizes look "right" and not oversized.
4. Click "Edit Profile" and change a field (e.g., zip code).
5. Verify the success message appears and data persists.
6. Intentionally leave a required field blank to verify the new error alert shows up.
